 the first aid kit and fire extinguisher are kept.</li></ul><h3>First aid</h3><ul><li><strong>First aid</strong>: First aid is the immediate care given to an injured person before professional help arrives. For a minor cut, wash the wound with clean water, apply pressure to stop bleeding, and cover it with a clean bandage. For a minor burn, cool the area under running water.</li></ul><h3>Hazards and how to prevent them</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Hazard</th><th>Possible injury</th><th>Prevention</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Wet floor</td><td>Slipping</td><td>Wipe spills immediately</td></tr><tr><td>Sharp knife</td><td>Cuts</td><td>Cut away from the body; store properly</td></tr><tr><td>Exposed wire</td><td>Electric shock</td><td>Report it; do not touch</td></tr><tr><td>Hot pan</td><td>Burns</td><td>Use pot holders or gloves</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Quick check</h3><ol><li>What is the difference between a hazard and a risk?</li><li>What does PPE stand for?</li><li>What should you do first for a minor burn?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answers</summary><ol><li>A hazard can cause harm; risk is the chance that it will.</li><li>Personal Protective Equipment</li><li>Cool the area under running water.</li></ol></details>', 1 FROM courses c
