naisin ang mabuti</strong> – magkaroon ng tamang kaalaman tungkol sa moral na isyu.</li><li><strong>Suriin ang sitwasyon</strong> – tingnan ang lahat ng detalye at posibleng bunga.</li><li><strong>Humingi ng payo</strong> – sa magulang, guro, o taong may malawak na karanasan.</li><li><strong>Magnilay at magpasya</strong> – pumili ng kilos na tugma sa likas na batas moral.</li></ol><blockquote><p><strong>Tandaan</strong></p><p>Kapag nag-aalinlangan ang konsensya, huwag munang kumilos hangga''t hindi malinaw kung tama ang gagawin.</p></blockquote><h3>Gawain</h3><p>Basahin ang sitwasyon: <em>Nakita mong kinokopya ng iyong matalik na kaibigan ang sagot ng iba sa pagsusulit.</em> Gamit ang apat na hakbang sa paghubog ng konsensya, isulat kung ano ang gagawin mo at bakit.</p><h3>Pagsusulit</h3><ol><li>Ano ang pangunahing prinsipyo ng likas na batas moral?</li><li>Ano ang dapat gawin kapag nag-aalinlangan ang konsensya?</li><li>Magbigay ng isang katangian ng likas na batas moral.</li></ol><details><summary>Ipakita ang sagot</summary><ol><li>Gawin ang mabuti, iwasan ang masama.</li><li>Huwag munang kumilos; alamin muna ang tama.</li><li>Alinman sa: pangkalahatan, hindi nagbabago, walang hanggan</li></ol></details>', 1 FROM courses c
WHERE c.course_code = 'HS10-ESP' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM modules x WHERE x.course_id = c.id AND x.module_number = 2);

UPDATE modules m JOIN courses c ON c.id = m.course_id
SET m.title = 'Music and Arts of the 20th Century', m.description = 'How music and art broke old rules and found new forms in the modern era.', m.content = '<blockquote><p><strong>By the end of this module, you should be able to:</strong></p><ul><li>Describe major styles of 20th-century music and art</li><li>Identify Filipino artists who shaped modern Philippine music and art</li><li>Compare traditional and modern styles</li></ul></blockquote><p>The 20th century brought world wars, new technology, and fast social change. Musicians and artists responded by experimenting with sounds, colors, and shapes that earlier generations had never tried.</p><h3>Part 1: Music</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Style</th><th>Main features</th><th>Composer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Impressionism</td><td>Soft, dreamy sounds that suggest moods and images</td><td>Claude Debussy</td></tr><tr><td>Expressionism</td><td>Intense emotion, harsh harmonies, no clear key</td><td>Arnold Schoenberg</td></tr><tr><td>Neoclassicism</td><td>Modern sounds in older, balanced forms</td><td>Igor Stravinsky</td></tr><tr><td>Electronic music</td><td>Sounds made or changed with machines and recordings</td><td>Karlheinz Stockhausen</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>Filipino composers</h4><ul><li><strong>Lucio San Pedro</strong> – composed "Sa Ugoy ng Duyan"; National Artist for Music.</li><li><strong>Antonio Molina</strong> – known for "Hatinggabi," blending Filipino melody with impressionist style.</li><li><strong>Ryan Cayabyab</strong> – modern composer of choral works, musicals, and popular songs.</li></ul><h3>Part 2: Arts</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Movement</th><th>Main features</th><th>Artist</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cubism</td><td>Objects broken into geometric shapes, shown from many angles</td><td>Pablo Picasso</td></tr><tr><td>Surrealism</td><td>Dreamlike, impossible scenes</td><td>Salvador Dalí</td></tr><tr><td>Pop Art</td><td>Images from ads, comics, and everyday products</td><td>Andy Warhol</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>Filipino modern artists</h4><ul><li><strong>Vicente Manansala</strong> – developed "transparent cubism," as in his paintings of jeepneys and vendors.</li><li><strong>Victorio Edades</strong> – called the father of modern Philippine painting.</li><li><strong>Fernando Amorsolo</strong> – a contrast to the modernists; famous for sunlit rural scenes.</li></ul><blockquote><p><strong>Compare</strong></p><p>Amorsolo''s paintings show the Philippine countryside realistically, with glowing light. Manansala''s cubist works break the same everyday subjects into overlapping shapes. Both are Filipino, but one is traditional and the other modern.</p></blockquote><h3>Activity</h3><p>Listen to "Sa Ugoy ng Duyan" and to a piece by Debussy. In a short paragraph, describe the mood of each and one difference in how they sound. Then sketch a simple object from your home in a cubist style.</p><h3>Quick check</h3><ol><li>Which music style creates soft, dreamy moods?</li><li>Who is called the father of modern Philippine painting?</li><li>What art movement uses images from ads and comics?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answers</summary><ol><li>Impressionism</li><li>Victorio Edades</li><li>Pop Art</li></ol></details>', m.published = 1
WHERE c.course_code = 'HS10-MAPEH' AND m.module_number = 1 AND m.updated_by IS NULL;
INSERT INTO modules (course_id, module_number, title, description, content, published)
SELECT c.id, 1, 'Music and Arts of the 20th Century', 'How music and art broke old rules and found new forms in the modern era.', '<blockquote><p><strong>By the end of this module, you should be able to:</strong></p><ul><li>Describe major styles of 20th-century music and art</li><li>Identify Filipino artists who shaped modern Philippine music and art</li><li>Compare traditional and modern styles</li></ul></blockquote><p>The 20th century brought world wars, new technology, and fast social change. Musicians and artists responded by experimenting with sounds, colors, and shapes that earlier generations had never tried.</p><h3>Part 1: Music</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Style</th><th>Main features</th><th>Composer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Impressionism</td><td>Soft, dreamy sounds that suggest moods and images</td><td>Claude Debussy</td></tr><tr><td>Expressionism</td><td>Intense emotion, harsh harmonies, no clear key</td><td>Arnold Schoenberg</td></tr><tr><td>Neoclassicism</td><td>Modern sounds in older, balanced forms</td><td>Igor Stravinsky</td></tr><tr><td>Electronic music</td><td>Sounds made or changed with machines and recordings</td><td>Karlheinz Stockhausen</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>Filipino composers</h4><ul><li><strong>Lucio San Pedro</strong> – composed "Sa Ugoy ng Duyan"; National Artist for Music.</li><li><strong>Antonio Molina</strong> – known for "Hatinggabi," blending Filipino melody with impressionist style.</li><li><strong>Ryan Cayabyab</strong> – modern composer of choral works, musicals, and popular songs.</li></ul><h3>Part 2: Arts</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Movement</th><th>Main features</th><th>Artist</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cubism</td><td>Objects broken into geometric shapes, shown from many angles</td><td>Pablo Picasso</td></tr><tr><td>Surrealism</td><td>Dreamlike, impossible scenes</td><td>Salvador Dalí</td></tr><tr><td>Pop Art</td><td>Images from ads, comics, and everyday products</td><td>Andy Warhol</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>Filipino modern artists</h4><ul><li><strong>Vicente Manansala</strong> – developed "transparent cubism," as in his paintings of jeepneys and vendors.</li><li><strong>Victorio Edades</strong> – called the father of modern Philippine painting.</li><li><strong>Fernando Amorsolo</strong> – a contrast to the modernists; famous for sunlit rural scenes.</li></ul><blockquote><p><strong>Compare</strong></p><p>Amorsolo''s paintings show the Philippine countryside realistically, with glowing light. Manansala''s cubist works break the same everyday subjects into overlapping shapes. Both are Filipino, but one is traditional and the other modern.</p></blockquote><h3>Activity</h3><p>Listen to "Sa Ugoy ng Duyan" and to a piece by Debussy. In a short paragraph, describe the mood of each and one difference in how they sound. Then sketch a simple object from your home in a cubist style.</p><h3>Quick check</h3><ol><li>Which music style creates soft, dreamy moods?</li><li>Who is called the father of modern Philippine painting?</li><li>What art movement uses images from ads and comics?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answers</summary><ol><li>Impressionism</li><li>Victorio Edades</li><li>Pop Art</li></ol></details>', 1 FROM courses c
